  "goodToKnow": "Kiefer is two different words. Der Kiefer is the jaw: der Oberkiefer, der Unterkiefer, and der Kieferorthopäde is the orthodontist most German teenagers visit for braces. Die Kiefer (plural die Kiefern) is a pine tree; the sandy soils around Berlin and in Brandenburg are full of Kiefernwälder. The gender tells you which is meant: der Kiefer bites, die Kiefer grows. Germany's most common trees are Fichte (spruce), Kiefer and Buche (beech)."
